body:
This was something that confused me as well. Here is some clarification.

## When panels switch

On Storybook's storybook, some stories will switch to a specific panel. This is intentional on some stories and is set at a story level. For example, in the `Addons/A11y/BaseButton` story, you can see a parameter is set to switch to the accessibility panel.

```javascript
export default {
  title: 'Addons/A11y/BaseButton',
  component: BaseButton,
  parameters: {
    options: { selectedPanel: 'storybook/a11y/panel' },
  },
};
```

This behavior is mysterious to me and probably shouldn't be used much. Thankfully, it is rare that a story will select a specific panel.

## Default Behavior

By default, the panels do not switch. For example, in Storybook, [navigate to one of the stories in the Basics category](https://5a375b97f4b14f0020b0cda3-bactiuydey.chromatic.com/?path=/story/basics-button--all-buttons). Switch to a different addon panel. Then, navigate to another story in that category.
